  "id": "pattern-theory",
  "term": "pattern theory",
  "definition": "Pattern theory, in this context, is the view that the self is best understood as a flexible, variable pattern rather than a fixed substance or something defined by one stable set of essential features. It describes self-consciousness as arising from the integration of embodied affective processes with intentional awareness, while remaining grounded in the body.",
